    "strict_token_count_and_mononym_logic": "The prompt explicitly commands: 'Identify the essay then the three people's names. Return 3 names separated by a comma \",\"'. Submitting 'John Milton' and 'Johann Gottlieb Fichte' literally submits six words across three slots, which is an authentic QA benchmark failure mode on strict token-counting regexes (`^[A-Za-z]+,\\s*[A-Za-z]+,\\s*[A-Za-z]+$`).",
    "source_language_integrity": "The majority's entire winning weapon against Pericles was 'document grounding'—what Borges wrote on the page. We turn this directly back on them: if our epistemic anchor is strict document grounding, we cannot justify Anglicizing 'Plutarco' into 'Plutarch' or hallucinating first names ('John', 'Johann Gottlieb') that do not appear anywhere in Borges's text.",
